  "raw": {
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Allendale-MI/Academic-Affairs-Specialist_R104996": {
      "title": "Academic Affairs Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position serves as the primary liaison on processes between the Provost’s Office, colleges, and Human Resources. This role manages hiring at the Provost Office level in Academic Affairs, advises leadership on policy development, participates in the Merit Review team and verifies that employee records in Workday are accurate and consistent across Academic Affairs. This position works collaboratively with the leadership team of each college and their support staff to ensure efficient, consistent, and effective human resources operations within Academic Affairs. Salary & Benefits: Minimum starting salary of $63,000, commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. PRIMARY DUTIES 1.    Manage the hiring processes between Academic Affairs and HR. 2.    Ensure accuracy and integrity of information between departmental and university HR systems (i.e., Workday) via established reconciliation procedures and reporting.  3.    Advise on the development and implementation of policies, procedures, and programs related to the continuous improvement of Academic Affairs HR processes in connection with the University mission, values, and goals. Recommend systems and procedures for internal controls as necessary. 4.    Design, maintain and prepare reports and comply with requests for information and audit processes.  5.    Evaluate the consistency of merit across colleges and identify how to best use limited resources to correct market and compression issues within and across units as a member of the Academic Affairs merit process team.  6.    Lead the collaborative monthly meetings between the Provost’s Office, Academic Affairs support staff, and HR. 7.    Review regular and affiliate faculty appointment letters, contract renewals, promotions, and tenure decisions for compliance with Academic Affairs and HR policy. Then update academic appointments in Workday. 8.    Maintain hiring data, sharing relevant information with Pew Faculty Teaching and Learning Center (FTLC) for faculty orientation and with IT for computer orders.  9.    Monitor the completion and documentation of terminal degrees for ABD faculty hires within the required timeframe.  10.    Serve on University committees as requested. 11.    Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree and a minimum of two (2) years’ related experience. Experience with implementing and interpreting HR processes for hiring, terminations, and pay raises. Attention to detail. Outstanding organizational skills and the ability to complete projects on a timely basis and manage multiple priorities. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to interact with students, faculty, and staff. Effective oral and written communication. Proficient with Microsoft Office. Experience working HR functions within an Enterprise Resource Program  PREFERRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Experience in higher education. Workday experience with HR processes Experience training others in processes in a corporate/higher ed environment How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume, these documents are required and a pplications missing required documents will not be considered   . The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact  Paul Isely ( iselyp@gvsu.edu ) .  If you need technical assistance,   please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .   Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.     Application Deadline:   Application   review   begins  Monday September 15, 2026, and t his posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Allendale-MI/Office-Coordinator---Office-of-the-Provost_R104951-1": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator - Office of the Provost",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position supports the Office of the Provost and the Academic Affairs Communications Team by coordinating office functions, assisting with scheduling and communications, and providing excellent customer service. This role serves as a key point of contact for the office and helps ensure the efficient day-to-day operation of administrative activities. Job Classification & Benefits: C3 Level. Minimum starting wage of $20.49 per hour Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Essential Functions: Manage and maintain the schedule for the Associate Vice President for Academic Affairs, Strategic Budget Management. Perform and coordinate scheduling tasks and support services associated with preparing and planning for meetings, special projects or other related duties for both internal and external contacts. Generate reports, presentation materials, spreadsheets and graphics, and other similar materials using computer systems. Support the Academic Affairs Communications Team, including editing and proofreading content; developing event invitations and newsletters using email marketing platforms (e.g., Emma); publishing and monitoring social media content; and assisting with event planning and execution. Maintain the Office the Provost website.  Assist with announcements, mailings, and publications for distribution. Supervise student employees. Process student employee payroll and maintain appropriate records. Manage front-office operations by greeting visitors, answering and routing incoming calls, and ensuring a positive experience for internal and external constituents. Manage the Office of the Provost email account and disseminate messages as appropriate. Provide excellent customer service to students, faculty, and staff. Manage office conference room schedule and securing room reservations. Maintain office and divisional contact and email lists. Order office supplies and process university forms. Other duties as assigned. Non-Essential Functions: Assist with special events. Serve as back up support for other support staff in the office. Required Qualifications: High school graduate or equivalent. Minimum of three years of relevant work experience. Experience with various computer software applications such as Microsoft Office and/or equivalent. Demonstrated experience to successfully operate office equipment. Data entry experience. Typing and spelling competency with grammar and proofreading skills. Possess strong verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience to successfully provide quality customer service Demonstrated experience to successfully work independently, organize own work and coordinate work activities of others. Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines. Demonstrated experience to successfully maintain satisfactory work performance and attendance records. Ability to successfully maintain positive intercultural and interpersonal relationships. Preferred Qualifications: Higher education experience. Supervisory experience. Website editing experience on CMS or other website software. Supervision Received: Receives general instruction from a designated supervisor but is generally expected to work independently. Supervision Exercised: Hire, train, supervise, schedule and coordinate the work of student employees and may act as lead worker to other PSS staff members within the department/unit/division.  How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume.   The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact  Mary Albrecht (albrechm@gvsu.edu) .  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.     Application Deadline:   Application closes  September 10, 2026 .   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Grand-Rapids-MI-Pew-Campus/Centralized-Client-Intake-Manager---MI-Small-Business-Development-Center_R104970": {
      "title": "Centralized Client Intake Manager – MI-Small Business Development Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Under the direction of the Michigan SBDC Lead Center leadership, the Centralized Client Intake Manager is a critical leadership role responsible for transforming the Michigan SBDC’s intake process from a regional \"patchwork\" into a high-performance, standardized statewide model. This individual will oversee a centralized team of Intake Specialists to provide a professional, consistent, and efficient \"front door\" for all clients. The Manager balances high-level systems orchestration—including AI integration and tech stack management—with daily team supervision to ensure every client is efficiently triaged and matched with the right consultant based on geography and expertise. This position is grant-funded and subject to the availability of funding. Salary & Benefits: $65,000; commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package   including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources, and tuition waiver effective on the date of hire.     Primary Duties:   1. Team Leadership & Management Direct Supervision: Provide daily leadership and coordination for a team of 3 to 5 full- or part-time Intake Specialists (contractors or students). Hiring & Onboarding: Lead the recruitment, hiring, and onboarding for the intake team. Training & Resource Development: Create and maintain all training materials, standardized scripts (including sorting and triage logic), and knowledge bases. Performance Governance: Conduct regular quality audits of Salesforce data entry and intake session notes to ensure adherence to statewide standardized protocols. Capacity Management: Manage the Intake Shift Schedule to ensure 100% coverage during business hours. Work alongside regional consultants and regional directors to manage scheduling systems. 2. Operational Excellence & Triage Governance System Ownership: Maintain the process document and the Statewide Consultant Matrix to ensure accurate client-to-consultant matching. Complex Case Escalation: Act as the final authority and decision-maker for \"special case\" client inquiries or system discrepancies that fall outside standard operating procedures. Workflow Management: Directly manage intake-specific workflows to eliminate regional variability and ensure a high-quality, uniform experience across all regions. Stakeholder Liaison: Serve as the central bridge between frontline intake personnel, Regional Directors, and the Lead Center to ensure functional alignment and transparency. 3. Tech Stack Orchestration & AI Integration Systems Alignment: Optimize the use of Salesforce, Google Workspace, Calendly, and Slack to identify and implement the most efficient tools for statewide scaling. AI Development: Lead the refinement of the Intake-specific Gems (such as Intake Session Note Summarizer) to ensure high-fidelity, consultant-ready data extraction. Calendar Compliance: Assist with the transition to Google Workspace for all intake sessions and use of Calendly to prevent double-bookings. 4. Data Analysis & Fiscal Accountability Metric Definition & Tracking: Establish and monitor meaningful conversion benchmarks (Lead-to-Consultant) and enforce adherence to the MI SBDC’s governance policy. Fiscal Modeling: Ensure all intake staff accurately log \"Contact Time\" and \"Prep Time\" to determine true operational cost-per-intake for future budget planning. Program Evaluation: Synthesize data and performance benchmarks into recommendations for continuous improvement for the client intake model.   Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, Organizational Leadership, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Supervisory Experience: Minimum of 2–3 years of experience directly supervising staff, with a proven track record of managing performance, coordinating team schedules, and fostering a collaborative work environment. Operational Management: Demonstrated experience managing professional operations, workflows, or customer-facing intake systems. Must show an ability to maintain high-quality service standards in a fast-paced environment. Process Orientation: Experience developing, implementing, or maintaining Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). The candidate must demonstrate an understanding of how to use documentation to ensure consistency across a team. Customer Success or Intake Operations: Minimum of 3 years of experience in high-volume customer-facing scheduling and service, where maintaining a high standard of professional \"first impression\" was critical. Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with a specific ability to navigate \"change management\" conversations and build consensus among stakeholders. Technical Literacy: Proficiency with digital productivity tools (such as Google Workspace or Microsoft 365) and a demonstrated ability to quickly learn and adopt new software, platforms, or database systems.   Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Matrix Management Experience: Experience managing workflows or personnel across multiple geographic regions or departments. Project Management: Experience moving a new program into a permanent, standardized operational model, including the development of Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Data & Fiscal Aptitude: Experience tracking operational metrics and labor hours to assist in budget forecasting and cost-per-unit analysis. Systemic Thinking (Triage Mindset): Proven ability to manage a strict project scope; specifically, the ability to distinguish between administrative/triage needs and substantive consulting or diagnosis. Technical Proficiency: Experience using a CRM (such as Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar) to manage data and workflows. High proficiency in Google Workspace and automated scheduling tools is a plus (e.g., Calendly).   Working Conditions: Flexible Work Arrangement (FWA): This position is eligible for a Flexible Work Arrangement in accordance with University policy. Primary Location: This role is designed as a Remote-First position to effectively manage and provide leadership across a statewide team. Hybrid Option: For candidates within commuting distance of a GVSU campus, the role allows two remote days per week and requires three days in the office. Operational Presence: The Manager is expected to maintain standard business hours (8:00 AM – 5:00 PM EST) to provide consistent leadership for the Centralized Client Intake team. Occasional travel for leadership meetings and annual conferences will be required. How to Apply (if applicable): Apply online at GVSU Careers to be considered; applicants must upload the following (in PDF format) to the online application ( five documents or five MB maximum ): 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Unofficial copy of transcript If selected for an interview, you will be asked to provide the names, phone numbers, and e-mail addresses of three professional references. You will also be required to submit official transcripts prior to the interview. If you have questions or need assistance, call Human Resources at 616-331-2215. Questions about this position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Erika Morrison,   morrerik@gvsu.edu . Sponsorship Disclosure (if applicable): Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. Application Deadline: Application closes September 11th, 2026. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. About the Department/Division • For details about Seidman College of Business, visit   www.gvsu.edu/seidman . • For details about the Unit, visit   www.michigansbdc.org . To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Muskegon-MI/Associate-Director-of-Entrepreneurial-Services---Muskegon-Innovation-Hub_R104878": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Entrepreneurial Services - Muskegon Innovation Hub",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position leads client-facing business development for the Muskegon Innovation Hub, from initial outreach through 1-on-1 coaching, driving the Hub's growth and its portfolio of success stories, with particular emphasis on developing high-growth technology companies from concept to commercialization and on serving early- through growth-stage businesses with limited access to capital, networks, or technical assistance. As the Hub's tactical lead for ecosystem relationship-building, this role is accountable for filling the Hub's pipeline of clients by partnering with community-based organizations that refer entrepreneurs to the Hub. The position is also responsible for designing and sustaining the coaching and client-lifecycle systems that allow the Hub's programs to operate efficiently and endure through staff transitions. Salary & Benefits:   Minimum starting salary of   $75,000 ,   commensurate   with experience     Comprehensive benefits package   including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness   resources   and tuition waiver effective on date of hire.   Primary Duties:   Fill the Hub's client pipeline across coaching, accelerator, and grant programs through direct outreach to entrepreneurs and small businesses, including early- through growth-stage businesses with limited access to capital, networks, or technical assistance. Serve as the Hub's tactical lead for ecosystem relationship-building across the six-county region, proactively establishing and maintaining collaborative relationships with GVSU faculty and staff, other entrepreneurial support organizations, economic development organizations, and service providers who scout and refer clients; Co-plan and coordinate partner-delivered programming with partners, and collect partner activity and outcome metrics for Hub reporting. Provide 1-on-1 coaching and mentoring to Hub clients in strategic business management, innovation, and growth planning, conducting needs assessments and co-creating actionable business plans that address each client's specific challenges and goals. Plan, develop, and lead the Hub's cohort-based accelerator program ElevateWest, including curriculum, cohort recruitment and onboarding, and program delivery. Connect clients to capital and financing across the ecosystem, providing direct coaching support for Business Accelerator Fund applications, including business-plan and executive-summary development in coordination with the Assistant Director. Design, document, and continuously improve sustainable coaching and client-lifecycle processes and systems—including client intake, coaching workflow, pipeline tracking, and a repeatable accelerator playbook—so that programs run efficiently across the team and sustainably Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge,   Skills   and Abilities:   Bachelor's degree in a relevant field. Minimum seven (7) years of business experience. Demonstrated ability to build and manage partnerships and stakeholder relationships across organizations. Experience providing 1-on-1 coaching or mentoring. Ability to articulate an understanding of traditional and emerging industries relevant to Michigan's economic recovery and future success. Excellent verbal, written, presentation, and negotiation skills. Resourceful and proactive in gathering information, sharing ideas, and building and sustaining programs and business processes and systems. Strong/advanced computer skills. Demonstrated organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and client relationships simultaneously. Preferred Knowledge,   Skills   and Abilities:   MBA or equivalent relevant post-graduate degree. Experience coaching early-stage or rural businesses with limited access to capital, networks, or technical assistance. Working familiarity with the Business Model Canvas. International Business Innovation Association’s Entrepreneur Center Manager or equivalent certification. Project Management Institute Certified Associate in Project Management or equivalent certification. Coaching certification or relevant training in business coaching methodologies. Grant or proposal writing experience. Five (5) years of entrepreneurial or intrapreneurial management experience. Working Conditions: Normal office environment. Some travel required. How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume.   Applications missing required documents will not be considered . The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact  search chair Tom Hopper at hoppert@gvsu.edu .  If you need technical assistance,   please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.     Application Deadline:   Application closes   September 10 at 11:59pm, 2026.   This   posting   may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Muskegon-MI/Business-Manager---AWRI_R104925": {
      "title": "Business Manager - AWRI",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSummary : This position is responsible for the financial operations of the Robert B. Annis Water Resources Institute (AWRI) and provides strategic input as a member of the AWRI administrative team. The role involves developing and implementing systems, protocols, and procedures to ensure that financial planning aligns with strategic objectives and priorities. Areas of responsibility include budget development, execution, and compliance; purchasing review; contract development, execution, and invoicing; and hiring and contract management of staff. This position includes close collaboration with AWRI administrative staff and the Executive Director. As a key member of the administrative leadership team, this position plays a critical role in advancing the Institute’s operational excellence and long-term sustainability. Salary/Benefits : Minimum starting salary of $60,720. The university offers an excellent comprehensive package that includes health/vision/dental plans, life insurance, retirement, sick/leave disability, tuition waiver, adoption resources, wellness coaching, and free access to campus fitness facilities, effective on date of hire. Family and child-care options on and off-campus are also available. Primary Duties Develop and implement long-term financial plans for the Institute to ensure financial sustainability. Develop and implement operational processes for the Institute that integrate with other University departments, including the Office of Sponsored Programs, Business and Finance Office, and Human Resources Manage a diverse funding model of contributed and earned revenues Institutional budget development and management Endowment and gift management, accounting, and reporting Grant budget development, management, reporting, and compliance Contract development, execution, and invoicing Process purchase orders, online invoices, and requisitions AWRI cost center assistant review of all expense reimbursement, purchasing, etc. Coordinate expense card reconciliation Manage hiring and contract management of staff Prepare monthly financial reports for the Executive Director Performs other duties as required/assigned by leadership Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Bachelor’s degree in accounting, business administration, or related field. Three (3+) years’ experience in the accounting or finance field. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with a collaborative and innovative team. Strong experience in financial management in environments using spreadsheet and database applications. Evidence of strong problem-solving and analytical skills. Evidence of ability to work independently as well as with others. Strong cultural competence, collaboration, and interpersonal skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrates high standards of work quality and integrity. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Federal and/or State grants management experience. Audit experience. Grant Management Certification (examples: CGFM, CGMS, Management Concepts Grant Management Certification, GPC, CRA, SRA). Certified Public Accounting credentials. University-based finance experience. Contract management experience. Experience using Workday. Department : The Annis Water Resources Institute (AWRI) is a world-class research facility situated on Muskegon Lake in Muskegon, MI, on the shores of Lake Michigan. The institute houses a dozen faculty, numerous research staff, and a robust graduate program. Located 30 miles from the main Grand Valley State University campus, AWRI maintains state-of-the-art analytical and molecular laboratories, a mesocosm facility, and two research vessels. Please visit the AWRI website (www.gvsu.edu/wri) for more information on our faculty, facilities, research programs, and educational/outreach initiatives. College : The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) is the largest college at Grand Valley, offering over 50 bachelor degrees and a growing number of advanced degrees in the natural and mathematical sciences, the fine arts and humanities, and the social sciences. CLAS is a student-centered and diverse learning community that engages in critical inquiry, extending knowledge to enrich and enliven individual and public life. Our faculty are active teacher-scholars committed to equitable, inclusive, career-connected, and community-engaged liberal arts and sciences education. There are many opportunities for collaboration within CLAS and across a broad group of partners on and off campus. We are interested in attracting a cohort of new faculty committed to these core values as we seek to foster a community where members from all backgrounds can live, learn, and thrive together. Campus/University:  Grand Valley University (GVSU) is a public comprehensive institution located in West Michigan with campuses in Allendale, downtown Grand Rapids, and Holland, plus centers in Detroit, Muskegon and Traverse City. The University attracts more than 22,000 undergraduate and graduate students with high quality programs and state-of-the-art facilities and has been nationally recognized for innovativeness and its contribution to students’ social mobility. The greater Grand Rapids metropolitan area has a population of around one million people, is affordable, and offers rich cultural amenities. Grand Valley is located within easy driving distance of Chicago, Detroit, Lake Michigan beaches, and many other superb summer and winter recreational venues. Information can be found at Community Resources - Human Resources - Grand Valley State University (gvsu.edu) . Grand Valley is highly rated for safety, sustainability, and veteran and LGBTQ friendliness, and is committed to supporting employees and their families in work-life balance. The university seeks to create an inclusive and diverse environment for faculty and students while promoting enrichment of society through excellent teaching, active scholarship, and service. More information can be found at Grand Valley State University (gvsu.edu) . How to Apply:  Apply online at GVSU Careers. A complete application must include: (1) a cover letter addressing qualifications and your motivation to take this position (2) résumé, (3) and contact information for three professional references. The online application will allow you to attach these documents electronically, in the same file location. If you need assistance, email Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu. Email questions about the position to: Stuart Jones, Executive Director of AWRI; jonesstu@gvsu.edu. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. Application Deadline:  The review process will begin September 14, 2026. The posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University thereafter. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Allendale-MI/Clinical-Medical-Assistant---Center-for-Health-and-Well-being_R104904": {
      "title": "Clinical Medical Assistant - Center for Health and Well-being",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position provides both clinical and administrative support to ensure smooth patient flow and an efficient front office experience. Responsibilities include checking vital signs, obtaining and documenting medical and social history, administering injections, performing venipuncture, scheduling, patient registration, referral coordination, and medical records processing. The role also involves greeting patients, verifying insurance, collecting payments, and coordinating care services. This position may mentor or precept students and volunteers assisting in any of these activities along with other duties as assigned. Salary & Benefits FTE: 0.87–1.0, negotiable based on candidate interest and availability. This position works approximately 40 hours per week during August–May, with the opportunity for a reduced summer schedule during June and July depending on the agreed-upon FTE. Salary will be prorated based on FTE, with a full-time 1.0 FTE salary range of   $34,000–$48,500 . Comprehensive benefits package  including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire.    Primary Duties Comply with appropriate regulations including HIPAA, CLIA, and OSHA. Follow established clinical and administrative protocols as applicable. Appropriately document patient interactions and medical information. Manage patient phone calls and messages as appropriate for scope of practice. Perform daily patient flow functions and front office duties, effectively multitasking in a fast-paced environment. Safely administer injections and perform venipuncture. Ensure that the registration area and telephones open promptly and that closing details are carried out. Greet clients/patients and obtain necessary documentation, ensuring accurate patient information and insurance verification. Collect payments for services and process billing information. Schedule and confirm patient appointments following established guidelines and conduct follow-up calls as necessary. Monitor daily schedules to ensure compliance with clinic guidelines and suggest improvements as needed. Keep accurate reports, patient statistics, and office productivity data for reporting purposes. Maintain office and medical supply inventory. Attend staff meetings, trainings, and clinic community activities. Provide care consistent with a patient-centered approach, addressing social determinants of health. Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Graduate of an accredited medical assistant training program or equivalent experience in a healthcare setting. Current Medical Assistant Certification in the State of Michigan. One (1) year working in a healthcare setting with electronic medical record experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Effective verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills with the ability to interact with diverse populations. Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment with a strong customer-service orientation. Ability to handle patient and organizational information in a confidential manner. Proficiency in a Windows-based computer system, including email, internet, and software such as Microsoft Word and Excel. Ability to perform detailed tasks with frequent interruptions and prioritize work effectively. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Vaccine/Allergy Injection Management College Health Experience  How to Apply Attach your cover letter and resume. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact  harmonka@gvsu.edu .  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at  hro@gvsu.edu .  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.  Application Deadline For full consideration, please apply by September 2. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.  Working Conditions Clinical office environment. Some travel may be required. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Grand-Rapids-MI-Pew-Campus/WGVU-Grant-Writer_R104931": {
      "title": "WGVU Grant Writer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position oversees grant funding opportunities that support WGVU goals and priorities in the areas of technology, education, IDEA, programming, community impact, and other areas as they arise. This role serves as a liaison between WGVU, the GVSU Office of Sponsored Programs, University Institutional Advancement, and GVSU Grants Accounting. Salary & Benefits: Salary range of $57,500 - $67,000, commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties Responsible for the grants administration process, including researching potential funders, evaluation of RFPs, overseeing management of funded projects, as well as tracking and reporting requirements. Write, review, and edit proposals to foundations and other potential funders. Identify, manage, and secure philanthropic gifts from private, corporate, and public foundations. Develop and maintain relationships with local, state, and federal funding agencies. Provide leadership for identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major foundation grant makers to increase gifts to WGVU. Work to establish long-term partnerships and strengthen existing relationships with foundation sector and community organizations. Serve as a liaison between WGVU, the GVSU Office of Sponsored Programs, University Institutional Advancement, and GVSU Grants Accounting. Manage a portfolio of foundation donors and prospects. Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Bachelor's degree in related field. Minimum of three to five (3-5) years of successful grant writing experience in nonprofit, public broadcasting, or educational setting. Proven experience in researching, writing, and administering grants. Ability to take initiative, collaborate, and use innovative techniques to prepare grant applications. Ability to design, develop, and implement funded projects. Ability to monitor budgets and expenditures to adhere to grant agreements. Ability to contribute to a work environment in which integrity, collaboration, respect, and a strong work ethic are valued. Experience with various computer software applications (Microsoft Office, Outlook, Teams, Monday.com, Raiser’s Edge/CRM, etc). Commitment to WGVU’s vision of diversity, inclusion, and equity. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills.  Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and meet deadlines. Ability to work within a collaborative multiplatform culture and environment. Ability to demonstrate professionalism, punctuality, and work self-sufficiently with little direction when required. Ability to maintain a flexible work schedule, including some nights, weekends, and holidays. Valid driver’s license and ability to work on location as needed. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Master’s degree. How to Apply: Attach your cover letter and resume. Applications missing required documents may not be considered . The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Terri Kenney at kenneyt@gvsu.edu .  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu . Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.   Application Deadline: Application closes September 7, 2026. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Allendale-MI/Assistant-Director-of-Academic-Community---Alumni-Engagement---Institutional-Advancement_R104928": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Academic Community & Alumni Engagement - Institutional Advancement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Academic Community & Alumni Engagement leads the strategy and coordination that strengthen connections between alumni and the university’s academic colleges. The role partners closely with deans, faculty, and academic staff to understand each college’s unique goals and to develop approaches that make alumni involvement accessible, meaningful, and sustainable. This position supports academic advisory boards, builds shared tools and practices, and helps connect colleges with alumni and community contributors in ways that enhance academic programs and student learning. The Assistant Director also guides strategic initiatives that increase visibility, reduce siloed efforts, and create consistent opportunities for alumni to stay engaged with their disciplines. The role collaborates closely with divisional and campus colleagues to ensure academic engagement efforts align with institutional priorities and elevate philanthropic interests.  Salary & Benefits:   Minimum starting salary of $61,500 , commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire.   Primary Duties Lead academic community and alumni engagement strategies that reflect university priorities and align with the unique needs and goals of each college.   Build strong relationships with deans, faculty, and academic staff to deepen alumni involvement in curricular and discipline specific initiatives.   Create shared tools, templates, and processes that help faculty and staff involve alumni in classroom engagement, experiential learning, and other discipline‑aligned academic volunteer opportunities.   Support academic advisory boards through guidance on recruitment, onboarding, member expectations, volunteer cultivation, and sustainable approaches to engagement and succession, ensuring alignment with college‑specific priorities.   Collaborate with colleges to identify opportunities for alumni involvement in mentoring related to academic programs and connect faculty and staff to campus‑wide mentoring resources and systems. Coordinate with campus colleagues to track academic engagement activity, emerging needs, and opportunities, and align academic‑based engagement events with the broader alumni engagement calendar to support cohesive planning across colleges. Collaborate with divisional colleagues and university partners to support experiential learning involving alumni.   Lead and support strategic initiatives that strengthen academic and community engagement across colleges and departments, including virtual opportunities that support college‑based teaching, learning, and alumni involvement.  Identify new ideas and opportunities that deepen alumni involvement in academic priorities and advance the Laker for a Lifetime philosophy, including collaboration with divisional colleagues to enhance philanthropic engagement.  Other duties as assigned.   Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Minimum of 2 to 3 years of full-time, post‑graduate experience in academic program support, alumni engagement, community partnership development, or related higher education roles. Bachelor’s degree. Strong ability to build collaborative relationships with deans, faculty, staff, alumni, and external partners. Skill in organizing complex work, managing multiple priorities, and adapting to the unique needs and expectations of different colleges and disciplines. Ability to design and maintain clear processes, tools, and shared resources that support consistent engagement across academic units. Ability to interpret alumni and engagement‑related data to inform planning, outreach, and strategy. Strong communication skills, including presenting, facilitating, and writing for academic and professional audiences. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Master’s degree, or a bachelor’s degree from Grand Valley State University. Experience advising, supporting, or coordinating academic advisory boards, college-based committees, or volunteer leadership groups. Experience collaborating with faculty or academic units to support classroom engagement, discipline‑specific alumni involvement, and experiential learning activities involving alumni or community contributors. Experience developing partnerships with academic departments, external organizations, or industry partners that support academic programs or student learning. Familiarity with engagement systems, CRM tools, or list management processes that support academic outreach and volunteer coordination. Experience with virtual engagement, workshops, or professional learning opportunities connected to academic programs. Working Conditions: Normal office environment. Some travel may be required How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume, these documents are required. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Institutional Advancement at advancement@gvsu.edu .  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu .     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.   Application Deadline:   Application closes September 7, 2026. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Grand-Rapids-MI-Pew-Campus/Finance---Grant-Specialist---MI-SBDC--Temporary-Hourly-_R104852": {
      "title": "Finance & Grant Specialist – MI-SBDC (Temporary Hourly)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Summary:  This position is a part-time adjunct position, not to exceed 29 hours per week (contingent upon funding) . This position will assist the Director of Finance and Grants with various financial reporting requirements, grant application document coordination, contract coordination & requirement, procurement requirements, invoice review and processing, monitoring multiple grant fund expenditures, and other administrative tasks as needed. This position assists with coordinating grant activities with 10 regional offices and supports projects such as the Business Accelerator Fund, Emerging Technologies Fund, SBA Cooperative Agreement, MEDC Core award, MEDC TECH award, and other federal, state, and project funds as required. Job Responsibilities: Work with MI-SBDC Director of Finance & Grants, to assist with finance monitoring and reporting. Maintain organized and accurate grant documentation for internal/external audits. Reconcile monthly grant information to the Lead Center’s systems/initiatives. Assist with financial processing including purchase order requisitions, invoice processing, and required documentation.  Monitor open Purchase Orders.  Track project expenditures; estimate burn down rates for various federal and state grants, gift and program income funds.  Assist with various state and federal reporting requirements.  Assist with contracts and agreements, including maintaining files and required documentation. Assist with audits (internal and external). Assist with year-end close out. Work in collaboration with GVSU Finance & Grants Management staff as required Work closely with the Director of Finance & Grants, assist with the annual SBA Cooperative Agreements application and documents requirements. Work closely with the Director of Finance & Grants, ensure compliance with federal and state grant requirements in conformance with federal, state, and university requirements including submission of timely (monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual) required reports. Ensure effective communication of related responsibilities to Lead Center staff and the regional offices and specialty teams. Work closely with the Director of Finance & Grants, assist with the sub-recipient monitoring functions for the SBDC providing support to the annual financial review. Support financial/compliance assistance to the regional hosts/service centers as needed and per the Subaward terms, and as requested by the Director of Finance & Grants. Provide monthly financial reporting forecasts, and insights for the Director of Finance & Grants to aid decision making. Performs other related duties as assigned by the Director of Finance & Grants. Job Qualifications: Federal and/or State grants management experience. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with a collaborative and innovative Leadership Team. A minimum of five years of relevant experience in working within the field of business accounting and/or grants and/or finance. Experience in developing and delivering management reports. Excellent oral and/or written communication skills. Strong attention to detail.   Strong experience in financial management in environments using spreadsheet and database applications.  Bachelor’s degree and/or commensurate experience. Preferred Qualifications: University-or public accounting finance experience. Audit experience Contract management experience. Experience using WorkDay. How to Apply (if applicable):  Apply online at GVSU Careers to be considered; applicants must upload the following (in PDF format) to the online application ( five documents or five MB maximum ): Cover letter Curriculum vitae Unofficial copy of transcript If selected for an interview, you will be asked to provide the names, phone numbers, and e-mail addresses of three professional references. You will also be required to submit official transcripts prior to the interview. If you have questions or need assistance, call Human Resources at 616-331-2215. Questions about this position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Jeanne LaSargeBono,  lasargej@gvsu.edu . To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Allendale-MI/Associate-GSRP-Preschool-Teacher---Children-s-Enrichment-Center--Temporary-_R104879": {
      "title": "Associate GSRP Preschool Teacher - Children's Enrichment Center (Temporary)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Associate Teacher provides safety, childcare, educational planning and implementation, and leadership within the classroom to support each child.   Job Type:   Temporary (Hourly) Compensation:  $17.00 per hour Essential Functions:   Act as the   secondary   care   provider and   instructor   for   assigned classroom   or   group .   I mplement   and   maintain   safety policies and procedures   with in   and outside   the classroom .     Assist   lead teacher in the   utilization   of   Creative Curriculum and Teaching Strategies Gold   assessment, observations, and   software.     Collaborate with   the lead teacher in the planning and implementation of weekly lesson plans that are developmentally   appropriate   and align with Creative Curriculum.   Assist   the   lead   teacher   in child observations and the collection of data in line with   the Great   Start Readiness Program ( GSRP )   and   Children’s Enrichment Center ( CEC )   requirements.   M aintain   appropriate   and professional relationships with families while   demonstrating   to families that their child/children’s needs are being best met.   Attend and help   facilitate   parent teacher conferences 2 times per school   year.   Accompany lead teacher on fall home visits required by GSRP.   Participate in   required   professional development opportunities   to   meet or exceed annual training requirements for   state   licensing ,   Great   Start to   Quality ,   and Great Start Readiness Program .   Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Qualifications:   An associate degree (AA) in early childhood education or child development or the equivalent; or A valid Center-Based Birth to Five CDA credential; or A valid Center-Based Preschool CDA credential .    Minimum   one   ( 1 )   year of experience in   a related   field.    Preferred Qualifications:   A bachelor degree in early childhood education or child development or the equivalent Infant/Child/Adult CPR certified Prior experience with Great Start to Quality (GSQ), Great Start Readiness Program (GSRP), and/or Teaching Strategies GOLD Working Conditions:  Preschool Classroom How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume.   Applications missing required documents will not be considered . The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact   Erin Korte, korteeri@gvsu.edu .  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. Application Deadline:   Application review begins August 14. T his posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
