    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Massage-Therapist---Campus-Health-Center--Temporary-_R104187": {
      "title": "Massage Therapist - Campus Health Center (Temporary)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Grand Valley Campus Health Center is seeking a skilled, student‑focused Massage Therapist to provide therapeutic, restorative, and preventive massage services to the GVSU community. This role supports the university’s mission of promoting holistic well‑being, stress reduction, injury prevention, and overall physical health within the campus community. This position is hourly and temporary. Compensation :     $34.00   per hour   Essential Functions:   Provide a range of therapeutic massage modalities. Conduct client intake, assessments, and individualized treatment plans. Maintain accurate and confidential client records. Identify contraindications and make referrals as needed. Educate clients on self‑care, stretching, posture, and stress management. Participate in wellness events and campus outreach. Maintain a sanitary and safe treatment environment. Manage appointment scheduling and documentation. Always uphold ethical and professional standards. Required Knowledge,   Skills   and Abilities:   State of Michigan Massage Therapist License. Completion of a 500+ hour massage therapy program. CPR/AED and First Aid certification or willingness to obtain.  Strong communication and professionalism.  Ability to work effectively with a diverse student population. Preferred Knowledge,   Skills   and Abilities:   Experience in clinical, wellness, college health, or athletic settings. Additional certifications (sports massage, myofascial release, etc.). Experience with electronic health record systems. Ability to assist with wellness programming or events. Working Conditions:   • Flexible hours with occasional evenings or weekend events. • Work in designated Health Center treatment rooms. • Some standing, bending, and lifting massage equipment up to 25 lbs. How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume.   The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact harmonka@gvsu.edu .   If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .     Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e. a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without the need of an employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of appointment.     Application Deadline:   Application review begins May 7. This   posting   may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
