    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Grand-Rapids-MI-Health-Campus/Information-Technology-Audio-Visual-Specialist_R104980": {
      "title": "Information Technology Audio/Visual Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role is integral to a team responsible for the support and maintenance of IT and audio-visual (AV) systems across various GVSU learning environments, including but not limited to classrooms, laboratories, simulation centers, and conference areas. The position involves a wide range of duties: operating, maintaining, distributing, installing, configuring, repairing, and upgrading electronic equipment to ensure peak performance. In alignment with IT Services' dedication to the GVSU community, the incumbent will swiftly and accurately address reported technical issues while providing essential end-user training and support. The role also encompasses comprehensive execution of AV projects, from initial evaluation and recommendation through design support, implementation, training, and ongoing maintenance. This position plays a direct role in supporting and advancing the university's Blue Dot initiative ecosystem, supporting the technology infrastructure, learning spaces, and instructional tools that enable the initiative's academic and student success objectives. In addition, the incumbent will help evaluate, pilot, deploy, and support emerging technologies, including extended reality (XR), virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR), and mixed reality (MR), as these tools are integrated into simulation, instruction, and experiential learning across campuses. This position will provide direct assistance to students, faculty, and staff on all computer, AV, and immersive technology issues. The incumbent will be expected to deliver prompt, efficient, and high-quality technical support across these diverse areas of responsibility. Salary & Benefits:  Minimum starting salary of $63,000; commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties:   1. Provide hands-on desktop and AV support across university facilities , precisely   classrooms, labs,   simulation   centers,   conference rooms, event spaces, and immersive/XR-enabled environments.   2. Provide post- implementation   s upport   to the   Blue Dot   project   through   routine   AV   technical   expertise , equipment readiness, space preparation, and responsive support for associated programs, pilots, and events.   3. Deploy, configure,   maintain , and troubleshoot XR/VR hardware, software, and peripherals ,   including headsets, tracking systems, content platforms, and network/workstation requirements ;   ensuring safe, sanitary, and reliable multi-user operation.   4. Supervise student employees (hiring, scheduling, mentoring, coaching) and develop and deliver user training, instructional materials, and onboarding for faculty on new and emerging technologies.   5. Collaborate with internal IT teams, faculty, instructional designers, and third-party vendors to resolve technical issues, assess   new technologies , and   participate   in the Simulation Center's monthly team meetings.   6. Maintain   accurate   inventory, configuration logs, and licensing for AV, simulation, and XR equipment across campuses, and support all learning modalities (in-person, remote, hybrid, distance, and immersive) by ensuring   optimal   environments and operational readiness.   7. Partner with the Project Management Office on IT/AV projects   throughout the univers ity,   including design, installation, documentation, specifications, and layouts ;   while researching emerging technologies, running proof-of-concept pilots, creating instruction manuals, and performing other duties as assigned.   Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:   High school graduate supplemented by a two-year degree in electronics or data communications, or an equivalent combination of training and experience.   Minimum of two years' experience in computer and peripheral equipment repair, with   demonstrated   working knowledge of TCP/IP networking protocols and AV systems.   Demonstrated knowledge of computer operating systems and electronics, with the ability to read and interpret complex electronic schematics and develop systems or signal flow diagrams.   Strong verbal and written communication skills, with a proven ability to   maintain   positive interpersonal relationships and provide quality customer service.   Ability to work independently and collaboratively ,   organizing   own   work, coordinating with others, and meeting deadlines under pressure.   Experience working with contractors and vendors to implement projects.   Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:   Bachelor's degree, ITIL foundations knowledge, and AVIXA Certified Technology Specialist (CTS) certification or equivalent experience.   Supervisory experience with a demonstrated   track record   of leading technical projects from planning through implementation.   Hands-on experience in video and audio technology ,   including compressed video distance learning principles, network cable and fiber optic termination, and manufacturers such as Neat, Logitech, Shure, Extron, Crestron, and Biamp.   Familiarity with XR/VR platforms and hardware, including deployment, device management, content distribution, and the technical requirements of immersive environments. D emonstrated ability to learn and support rapidly evolving technologies in   a higher education   environment, with flexibility to work non-standard hours as needed .   How to Apply:   Attach your cover letter and resume.   The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact  Lauren Glynn ( glynnla@gvsu.edu ) .  If you need technical assistance,   please contact Human Resources at   hro@gvsu.edu .     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.   Application Deadline:   Application   review   begins   September 21, 2026  and t his posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.   To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Grand-Rapids-MI-Pew-Campus/WGVU-Education-Engagement-Specialist_R105005": {
      "title": "WGVU Education Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position works within the WGVU broadcast area to build relationships and promote WGVU, PBS, PBS KIDS, NPR, and MLC programming and resources, while also leveraging curricular and digital learning tools to further engage and support educators, students, and families around equitable education outcomes. Salary & Benefits: Minimum starting salary range of $45,500, commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties Build relationships with WGVU viewing-area education service organizations, school districts, schools, teachers, families, and other partners by leveraging a focus on curriculum to promote the Michigan Learning Channel (MLC), WGVU Education, PBS, PBS KIDS, NPR, and other public media programs and resources. Promote public media resources and partnerships, along with programs and resources associated with WGVU Education, Michigan Learning Channel (MLC), PBS KIDS, and PBS LearningMedia. Plan, coordinate, implement and run program and event logistics in coordination with partner organizations, including workshops, special events, trainings, WGVU and GVSU events, community partner events, and more in alignment with school calendars, local events, and opportunities tied to specialized audiences. Implement K-12 special events, professional learning, workshops, and trainings around MLC, WGVU, PBS KIDS and PBS assets to support educators (and families) in curriculum integration and classroom or home use. Collect testimonials, data and best practices on how students, educators and families are using public media assets to support literacy, math, media literacy, youth voice, digital citizenship, storytelling, and content creation. Collect and organize all data required for quarterly grant and funder reporting. Participate in the coordination, planning and implementation of Education Department program work, including social media and weekly education newsletter content; webpage content; PBS LearningMedia content projects; PreK-12 professional learning events; education and community events; family engagement opportunities; and proposals and grant work. Maintain a current understanding of effective educational pedagogies and best practices; local and national education issues/policies; EdTech trends, apps, platforms, and tools; and Michigan and National K-12 Academic Standards. Support other WGVU staff, departments, and events, as needed. Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Bachelor’s degree in education. Secondary (grades 5-12) classroom teaching experience. Experience with integration and implementation of current digital tools and media in classroom instruction, student learning, and/or student work/outcomes. This may include Instructional Design, Ed Tech and other tools and resources (either in the classroom or as part of a school or district role). Ability to manage time and resources while balancing multiple projects and deadlines strategically and effectively. Comfortable speaking publicly and presenting to large groups while using digital tools. Commitment to GVSU’s Core Competencies.  Commitment to WGVU’s vision of diversity, inclusion, and equity. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills.  Ability to work within a collaborative multiplatform culture and environment. Ability to demonstrate professionalism, punctuality, and work self-sufficiently with little direction when required. Ability to maintain a flexible work schedule, including some nights and weekends. Valid driver’s license and ability to work on location as needed. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with literacy and/or ELA instruction is highly preferred. Content creation experience for education/classroom applications. Community and partner engagement experience. Experience with Microsoft Workplace tools, Google for education tools, and Canva. Experience with Zoom or other virtual conferencing platforms. NBCT or State Teaching Certification. How to Apply: Attach your cover letter and resume. Applications missing required documents will not be considered . The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Terri Kenney at kenneyt@gvsu.edu.  If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu . Application Deadline: Application closes September 22, 2026. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Battle-Creek-MI/Battle-Creek-Youth-Program-Specialist_R104882": {
      "title": "Battle Creek Youth Program Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position is responsible for developing and overseeing summer camps, after-school programs, and other activities for K-12 students in the Battle Creek area, as well as overseeing the 8th Grade Pathways to GVSU program. This role requires a passionate individual dedicated to creating engaging and educational programs that support students' academic and personal growth. Salary & Benefits: Minimum starting salary of $60,000, commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties: Development of Summer Camps: Program Design: Design and implement engaging and educational summer camp programs for K-12 students, creating comprehensive schedules, lesson plans, and activities. Staff Management: Recruit, train, and supervise camp staff and volunteers, ensuring a high-quality, safe, and enjoyable camp experience. Regulatory Compliance: Ensure all summer camp programs comply with relevant safety and health regulations, maintaining a secure environment for all participants. After-School Program Development: Program Development: Develop and oversee after-school programs tailored to the diverse interests and needs of K-12 students, providing enriching and supportive environments. Logistical Coordination: Manage program logistics, including location(s), transportation, and materials, to ensure seamless operations. Community Collaboration: Collaborate with local organizations and community partners to enhance program offerings and provide comprehensive support to students. Impact Assessment: Track attendance and assess the impact of after-school programs on student development, using findings to refine and improve the programs. 8th Grade Pathways to GVSU Program Oversight: Leadership: Lead the 8th Grade Pathways to GVSU program in Battle Creek with a focus on addressing the unique needs of students, ensuring it aligns with educational best practices and program objectives. Curriculum Development: Develop and implement a dynamic curriculum and engaging activities that support the program's goals and foster student growth. Coordination and Collaboration: Facilitate smooth program operations by coordinating with teachers, parents, school administrators, and University stakeholders, Academic Deans for college visits, admissions, financial aid, social justice centers, athletics, and other relevant units. Program Evaluation: Monitor and evaluate program effectiveness, using data-driven insights to implement necessary improvements and maintain records of student progress and program participation. Expansion Strategies: Explore and execute strategies to expand the program to additional partner schools and community organizations, enhancing the program’s reach and impact. Program Administration: Resource Management: Manage budgets and resources effectively, ensuring programs are cost-effective, sustainable, and aligned with financial goals. Funding Opportunities: Seek and secure funding opportunities through grants and partnerships to support and expand program initiatives. Promotion and Outreach: Promote programs through various channels to ensure high participation rates, engaging the community and stakeholders effectively. Data Analysis: Collect and analyze data to report on program outcomes and impact, using insights to drive program enhancements and demonstrate success. Community Engagement: Relationship Building: Foster strong, positive relationships with students, parents, school staff, and community members and organizations, creating a supportive and collaborative network. Event Organization: Organize events and activities to showcase student achievements and program successes, highlighting the impact of the programs. Liaison Role: Serve as a liaison between the school district and community organizations, facilitating communication and cooperation to support student development and program goals. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Bachelor’s degree in Education, Youth Development, or a related field. Minimum of three (3) years of dedicated experience in educational program development, youth programs, or related areas, with a proven track record of success. Demonstrated expertise in organizational and project management skills, with the ability to oversee multiple projects simultaneously and meet deadlines consistently. Exceptional communication and interpersonal abilities, capable of engaging effectively with students, parents, and colleagues. Extensive experience working with K-12 students in educational or recreational settings, particularly in the Battle Creek area, fostering a supportive and enriching environment. Strong commitment to and experience in working with diverse populations, including first-generation students and low-income learners, ensuring inclusive and equitable educational opportunities. Strong ability to work collaboratively with a diverse group of stakeholders, including educators, community leaders, and parents, to achieve common goals. PREFERRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Master’s degree in Education, Public Administration, Nonprofit Management, or a related field. Proven experience in grant writing and fundraising, successfully securing funding for educational programs and initiatives.  In-depth knowledge of local community resources and organizations in Battle Creek, with established connections and a strong network within the community. How to Apply: Attach your cover letter and resume, applications missing required documents will not be considered. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Al Shifflett at shifflea@gvsu.edu . If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e. a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without the need of an employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of appointment Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on Monday September 21, 2026, and the posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the university. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Executive-Director--Student-Success_R104997-1": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Student Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGrand Valley State University is searching for an Executive Director for Student Success. We are looking for a collaborative leader and strategic thinker who has a deep understanding of academic advising and student success. This role provides oversight and leadership for the First-Year Academic Experience, Student Academic Success Center, Laker Academic Success Center, and Exploratory Advising Center, and is also responsible for campus coordination and support of academic advising. This position serves as campus administrator for student success software (Navigate), including supervision of the Student Success Software Specialist. The successful candidate will possess at least a Master’s degree, preferably in higher education administration, student development or a related field. Salary & Benefits: Minimum starting salary of $114,000, commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties: 1.    Serve as campus lead for academic advising; develop advising systems, policies, and procedures across the campus that provide equitable access to advising services as well as the stated outcomes of advising.  Coordinate campus efforts to support and enhance academic advising as a key student success strategy.  2.    Serve as campus academic representative for software and technologies related to advising and student success.  Work closely with Information Technology, the Office of the Registrar, Enrollment Development, and Student Affairs on the integration of technologies that support advising and student success.  3.    Provide leadership, oversight, and supervision for the Student Academic Success Center, Laker Academic Success Center, Exploratory Advising Center and the Student Success Software Specialist. Provide guidance on support for program offerings, staffing, budgeting, and assessment. 4.    Oversee faculty-led student success initiatives including the First-Year Academic Experience and related course offerings, Student Success Network, Linked Courses/Learning Communities, and academic advising at New Student Orientation. Supervise the faculty director of the First-Year Academic Experience. Ensure all faculty-led initiatives are integrated into overall institutional efforts to enhance student success. 5.    Lead Academic Affairs coordination with the Oliver Wilson Scholars (OWS) program. 6.    Collaborate with Institutional Analysis on the development and implementation of student success data including efforts to identify students needing support and assistance.  Work with campus partners to ensure that students respond to these efforts and that follow-up connections with identified students are effective. 7.    Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: •    Master’s degree is required, preferably in higher education administration, student development or related field. •    Minimum of ten (10) years of related work experience in the area of student success. •    Administrative or other significant academic leadership experience.  •    Experience leading and supervising professional staff, including setting expectations, providing feedback, supporting professional development, and fostering a collaborative team environment. •    Experience working with students, staff, and faculty of diverse backgrounds. •    Strong organizational skills. •    A flexible and collegial work and communication style. •    Comfort with high levels of responsibility and accountability. •    Excellent oral and written communication skills. •    Excellent analytic ability. •    Prior experience working in higher education. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: •    In progress or earned doctorate, preferably in higher education administration, student development or related field. •    Deep understanding of best practices related to student success and the ability to use data to make decisions that support student success. •    Direct experience in using technology systems and data dashboards to guide student success efforts. •    Experience integrating career design and career readiness into student success strategies, helping students connect their academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning to meaningful career pathways. •    Experience leading or developing first-year advising programs that support students’ transition to college, foster belonging and engagement, and promote academic success, persistence, and degree completion.   How to Apply: A complete application must include: (1) a cover letter addressing qualifications and motivations to take this position, (2) resume, and (3) contact information for 3 professional references. Applications missing required documents will not be considered. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Donovan Anderson, andersdo@gvsu.edu. If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. Application Deadline: Application review begins on September 23, 2026. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University.    To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Assistant-Professor---Robert-B-Annis-Water-Resources-Institute_R105015": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Robert B. Annis Water Resources Institute",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nSummary: The Robert B. Annis Water Resources Institute (AWRI) at Grand Valley State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Water Resources to begin Fall 2027. Applicants are expected to have a Ph.D. in ecology & evolution, freshwater science, aquatic chemistry & toxicology, limnology, ecological engineering, or a closely related field. We welcome applications from researchers working at any spatial scale, in any freshwater system (lakes, rivers, streams, wetlands, or groundwater), at any level of biological or environmental organization, and using any mode of inference, from empirical to computational. Applicants who can augment our existing strengths in conservation and restoration ecology, environmental sensing and detection, human and environment interactions, and aquatic biogeochemistry and contaminants are particularly encouraged to apply. The mission of AWRI is to integrate research, education, and outreach to enhance and preserve freshwater resources. Over our 40-year history we have built a culture of interdisciplinary collaboration, deep community engagement, and a commitment to faculty and staff well-being. Individuals from all backgrounds, including from underrepresented groups, are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates must be able to effectively engage with students, colleagues, and community members with a broad range of backgrounds and experiences. Required Qualifications and Education: Ph.D. focused in ecology and evolution, freshwater science, aquatic chemistry and toxicology, limnology, ecological engineering, or closely related field. A demonstrated record of publishing quality research in their field of expertise. Potential for successful college-level teaching and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students in research. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, such as the ability to interact with others with respect and cultural humility. Preferred Qualifications and Education: Success obtaining extramural funding for research. A desire to work in a collaborative, interdisciplinary environment. Interest in engaging in a robust community engagement and education program. Responsibilities:  Tenure-track faculty in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences are typically hired on nine-month contracts. Tenure-track faculty at the Annis Water Resources Institute (AWRI) will balance their teaching and research workloads in collaboration with the AWRI Executive Director. A minimum of three-credit hours of teaching is required per year and remaining workload is allocated to research with specific expectations defined using credit-hour equivalents. Tenure-track faculty are also expected to engage in service within and beyond the institution, as well as community engagement activities that suit the successful candidate's interests and the department’s needs. Salary & Benefits:  Minimum starting salary: $80,000; commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package , including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire.   Department: AWRI is a world-class research facility situated on Muskegon Lake in Muskegon, Michigan, on the shores of Lake Michigan. The institute houses a dozen faculty, numerous research staff, and a robust M.S. program in Biology with an aquatic science emphasis. Located 30 miles from the main Grand Valley State University campus, AWRI maintains state-of-the-art analytical and molecular laboratories, a mesocosm facility, and two research vessels. Please visit the AWRI website ( www.gvsu.edu/wri ) for more information on our faculty, facilities, research programs, educational programs, and outreach initiatives. College: The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) is the largest and most intellectually diverse college at Grand Valley State University, offering over 50 bachelor’s degree programs, badges, and certificates spanning the natural and mathematical sciences, the fine arts and humanities, and the social sciences. CLAS is a student-centered learning community that welcomes individuals from various backgrounds and engages in critical inquiry, extending knowledge to enrich and enliven individual and public life. Our faculty are active teacher-scholars committed to offering students an accessible and community-engaged liberal arts and sciences education that prepares them for meaningful careers. There are many opportunities for collaboration within CLAS and across a broad group of partners on and off campus. We are interested in attracting a cohort of new faculty committed to these core values as we seek to foster a community where members from all backgrounds can live, learn, and thrive together. University: Grand Valley State University (GVSU) is a public comprehensive institution located in West Michigan. GVSU has multiple campuses—the Valley Campus in Allendale, Michigan; the City Campus located in downtown Grand Rapids; and several regional centers, including AWRI in Muskegon, Michigan. The University attracts 22,000 undergraduate and graduate students with high-quality programs and state-of-the-art facilities and has been nationally recognized for innovativeness. The greater Grand Rapids metropolitan area has a population of more than one million people, is affordable, and offers rich cultural amenities. GVSU is located within easy driving distance of Chicago, Detroit, Lake Michigan beaches, and many other superb summer and winter recreational venues. Information on Community Resources can be found on the Community Resources page of the GVSU Human Resources website . How To Apply: Apply online at GVSU Careers . To be considered for the position, applicants must upload the following items to the online application: A cover letter addressing qualifications and your motivation to join AWRI Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement The names and contact information of three references   The online application will allow you to attach these documents electronically to the same file location. Applicants selected for interviews will be required to submit official transcripts prior to the interview. If you need assistance, email Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu . Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Stuart Jones, Allen and Helen Hunting Executive Director of AWRI at jonesstu@gvsu.edu. Application Deadline: Consideration of applicants will begin on October 9, 2026. The posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University thereafter. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Accountant---Business-and-Finance_R105037": {
      "title": "Accountant - Business and Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThis entry-level position processes financial reports, prepares journal entries, and maintains accurate accounting records to support the operations of the Financial Reporting team. Salary and Benefits: $50,000-$60,000; commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources and tuition waiver effective on date of hire.   Primary Duties: Department Transfer Requests Manage the inbox for campus-created department transfer Requests. Prepare and enter departmental journal entries, reviewing requests for appropriateness, proper authorization, and compliance with internal standards and policies. Payroll Accounting Adjustments Prepare and process payroll accounting adjustments, ensuring accurate accounting and appropriate worktag assignments. Financial Reporting Prepare and assist with monthly and quarterly financial reports, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and timely distribution. General Fund Accounting Lead accounting activities for the general fund, including monitoring activity, reviewing transactions, and ensuring compliance with applicable accounting standards and institutional policies. Charge-Back Activity Prepare and coordinate various monthly charge-back activities and serve as the primary contact for campus-wide accounting support related to these activities. Worktag Corrections Research and correct program code and other worktag mismatches or missing worktags to ensure accurate financial reporting and accounting. Prepaid Expense Accounting Lead the monitoring and reconciliation of prepaid expenses, ensuring accurate balances and timely recognition of expenses. Bank Desk Support Provide back-up support for bank desk functions, including cash receipt processing and related accounting activities. Prepaid Expense Accounting Lead the monitoring and reconciliation of prepaid expenses, ensuring accurate balances and timely recognition of expenses. Other Duties Perform other duties as required or assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Bachelor’s degree with a Major in Accounting Excellent communication skills with the ability to effectively interact with students, faculty, and staff. Outstanding organizational skills and the ability to complete projects on a timely basis and manage multiple priorities Attention to detail and reconciliation experience Proficient with Microsoft Office software suite, in particular Excel Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: A minimum three years of related experience with duties outlined above. Working Conditions:  Normal office environment. Some travel may be required. How to Apply:  Attach your resume. Applications missing required documents will not be considered if applicable. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact department Karen Mushong , mushongk@gvsu.edu,  or 616-331-2233. If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.   Application Deadline:  Application closes October 2, 2026 . This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
