    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Muskegon-MI/Deckhand-on-the-WG-Jackson--Temp-Hourly-_R105017": {
      "title": "Deckhand on the W.G. Jackson (Temp Hourly)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nJob Summary : The deckhand's primary role is to maintain safety and security onboard the WG Jackson during cruises. They inspect and operate several pieces of equipment throughout the day and and follow direction of the captain to ensure safe operation of the vessel. Compensation : $19.00 per hour. This position is not eligible for benefits.   Essential Functions Represent Grand Valley State University and the Annis Water Resources Institute in a professional matter Maintain proper vessel security I.A.W. Ref (a) Carry out duties of the Deckhand as outlined in the PMS program I.A.W. Ref (b) Report vessel deficiencies to the on duty Captain and correct same as required Take the lead in all emergency evolutions including, man overboard, fire fighting, taking on water etc. Maintain the sanitation, overall condition, appearance, and safety of the vessel Master the proper operation of all weight handling equipment Monitor the safe and proper operation of all vessel weight handling and scientific equipment Complete routine inspections and maintenance as directed by the Fleet Captain Become familiar with the vessel’s radio, navigation equipment, and controls in order to call for assistance and safely return the vessel to port in case of an emergency Master the required safety drills Work at the direction of the Captain to ensure the safe operation of the vessel Handle lines as required Monitor aft deck safety Learn the proper operation and maintenance of scientific equipment used on the aft deck, including bathythermographs, water samplers, dredges, corers, plankton nets, trawl nets, and CTD’s Be knowledgeable about and respond to questions from passengers regarding safety, educational programs, and equipment Maintain aft deck discipline when no science instructor is present Ensure all ship’s equipment is secured properly and ready for sea Learn, follow, and promote proper safety procedures I.A.W. Ref (c) Assist science instructors and researchers as required, in coordination with the on duty Captain Act as a host and guide for occasional dockside tours and demonstrations Other duties as assigned by the Vessel Captain and Fleet Captain Required Qualifications: Ability to swim and comfort working on and around open water Ability to stand for extended periods, climb ladders, and work on a moving deck in wet, cold, or hot conditions Ability to follow verbal and written instructions from the Captain quickly and accurately, especially during drills and emergencies Willingness to take charge of emergency evolutions (man overboard, fire, flooding) after training and stay calm under pressure Strong attention to detail for inspections, equipment checks, and securing gear before departure Ability to work as part of a small crew and communicate clearly with the Captain, instructors, and fellow crew Comfort interacting with the public, including K-12 students, teachers, and community groups, and answering basic questions about safety and equipment Willingness to perform cleaning, painting, and routine maintenance tasks Mechanical aptitude and willingness to learn the operation of scientific sampling equipment Ability to represent GVSU and AWRI professionally in appearance, language, and conduct How to Apply : Attach your resume. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Eric Hecox ( hecoxe@gvsu.edu ). If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Admissions-Recruiter_R104919": {
      "title": "Admissions Recruiter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThis position will represent GVSU to prospective students, parents, secondary school counselors and other individuals or organizations involved in the college selection process. This position will manage assigned recruitment territory through prospect relationship management, leveraging partnerships, relationships, and admissions and enrollment data to maintain consistent recruitment activity, to increase prospective student interaction, and influence admission yield. Salary & Benefits:  $51,000 - $55,000, commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources, and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Primary Duties: Represent GVSU both on and off-campus to prospective students, parents, secondary school counselors, and other individuals or organizations involved in the college selection process. Advise prospective applicants on the admissions process, academic programs, support resources, and opportunities at the university through in-person and virtual appointments, small group presentations, phone calls, and emails. Manage assigned recruitment territory through prospect relationship management, leveraging partnerships, relationships, and admissions and enrollment data to maintain consistent recruitment activity, to increase prospective student interaction, and influence admission yield. Review materials submitted by applicants for the purposes of making admission decisions. Develop and implement recruitment and yield projects as assigned. Participate in information sessions, open houses, and other recruitment and yield events. Perform other duties as required/assigned by leadership. Required Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities: Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of two (2) years of experience in customer service, recruitment, education, sales, or related field. Strong cross-cultural skills. Strong presentation, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Commitment to GVSU’s vision of inclusion and equity.  Valid driver’s license and ability to travel to remote locations and to load and transport admissions materials, displays and other equipment. Ability to work evening and weekend hours required throughout the year, especially during the fall travel season. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities: Higher education experience. Experience with customer relationship management systems (CRM). College/university admissions experience or experience working with middle school or high school audiences. Bilingual in Spanish . Working Conditions: Monday through Friday, with evening and weekend work required throughout the year. Admissions recruitment occurs primarily by in-person appointments, but also by small group presentations, zoom appointments, phone calls and emails. Extensive travel is required. Department/Division: Admissions Office, Enrollment Development and College Futures Campus: Allendale, MI How to Apply: A cover letter and resume are required. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. Apply online at GVSU Careers . If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Faye Spears at spearsf@gvsu.edu . If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu . Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future. Application Deadline:  Review of applications will begin immediately, and the posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the university. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
    },
    "https://gvsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Allendale-MI/Admissions-Processor---Admissions-and-Recruitment_R105043": {
      "title": "Admissions Processor - Admissions and Recruitment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThis position will provide customer service and support for all stages of application processing which would include reviewing and processing admission applications for completion, data entry, document management, reviewing official transcripts, computing and inputting GPA’s, processing transfer equivalencies, and inputting test scores. The position will follow documented application requirements and established policies and procedures to effectively process applications. Salary & Benefits:  C3 Level. Minimum starting wage of $20.49 per hour Comprehensive benefits package including medical, vision, dental, life insurance, generous employer retirement contributions, wellness resources, and tuition waiver effective on date of hire. Essential Functions: Process, monitor and maintain admission applications from beginning to end Responsible for recruit and application data entry Process and maintain transfer equivalencies, application decisions, various calculations, and student records Prepare and mail appropriate correspondence to applicants Assist students, parents, staff, and faculty on the telephone, online, and in person Provide information and complete transactions as necessary Interpret regulations and procedures and respond appropriately Use information provided by computerized reporting to monitor and maintain the quality and accuracy of data Work with multiple data systems in the test and production environments Supervise student employees Other related duties as assigned Required Qualifications: High school graduate or equivalent Minimum of three years of relevant work experience Experience with various computer software applications such as Microsoft Office and/or equivalent Demonstrated experience to successfully operate office equipment Data entry experience Typing and spelling competency with grammar and proofreading skills Possess strong verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated experience to successfully provide quality customer service Demonstrated experience to successfully work independently, organize own work, and coordinate the work activities of others Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines Demonstrated experience to successfully maintain satisfactory work performance and attendance records Ability to successfully maintain positive intercultural and interpersonal relationships Preferred Qualifications: Some college course work Higher education experience Supervisory experience Experience with a CRM System (Customer Relationship Management System), such as Slate Prior experience working with international transcripts Supervision Received:  Receives general instruction from a designated supervisor but is generally expected to work independently. Supervision Exercised:  Hire, train, supervise, schedule, and coordinate the work of student employees and may act as lead worker to other PSS staff members within the department/unit/division. Department/Division: Admissions and Recruitment Office, Enrollment Development and College Futures Campus: Allendale, MI How to Apply: Attach your cover letter and resume. Applications missing required documents will not be considered. The system will allow you to attach these documents electronically. Apply online at GVSU Careers . If you have questions about the position or the posting, please contact Faye Spears at spearsf@gvsu.edu . If you need technical assistance, please contact Human Resources at hro@gvsu.edu . Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States and must not require sponsorship now or in the future.   Application Deadline:  Application closes October 8, 2026 at 11:59p.m.. This posting may be closed at any time at the discretion of the University. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  Must have the physical stamina to work long hours and/or more than 5 days per week.  The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The information contained in this job description is for compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act as amended by the ADA Amendment Act (2008), Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and other applicable federal and state laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of disability. GVSU will provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. See   www.gvsu.edu/equalopportunity/ . TDD Callers: Call Michigan Relay Center at 711 (in State) or 1-800-833-7833 (out of State).   Grand Valley State University is an Antidiscrimination/Equal Opportunity Employer, which includes providing equal opportunity for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. University policy extends protections to additional identities."
